# Local review screenshots, produced by UI review sessions. Never part of the
# submission; kept out so `git add -A` cannot ship one.
review-*.png

# Internal review write-ups. These belong in .private/ (HANDOFF §3.12); ignored
# at the repo root as a backstop so `git add -A` cannot ship one into the
# submission. Narrow paths, so a deliberate doc is never caught by accident.
# Anchored AND unanchored on purpose. Both files cite .private/ paths by name,
# and a copy of either under docs/ walked past the anchored form -- which matters
# more here than it looks, because scripts/package-offline.sh seals the bundle
# with `git archive HEAD`, so anything committed once ships in every bundle after.
/DEVOPS_REVIEW.md
/REVIEW_PLAN.md
DEVOPS_REVIEW.md
REVIEW_PLAN.md

# The internal hiring-review corpus, same block and same reason. Eighty-one files
# -- lane review notes, agent transcripts, a dress-rehearsal report, a presenter's
# demo script -- were untracked and stageable until 2026-09-28, when they moved
# under .private/; `git check-ignore` matched none of them, so nothing but care
# stopped a `git add -A` from committing them, and `git archive HEAD` (which
# scripts/package-offline.sh seals the bundle with) would then have shipped them
# to every air-gapped host afterwards.
#
# These patterns are unanchored, so they match at the root and under docs/ alike,
# which is where the corpus was split. The two directory rules were withheld in
# the commit that moved these files, because .gitignore does not untrack anything
# and a pattern over docs/rehearsal-review/ would have shadowed the two paths
# still tracked there at the time. That reason expired in the same commit: it
# untracked them, `git ls-files docs/rehearsal-review` is empty, and so is
# `git ls-files -i -c --exclude-standard` after these rules. A backstop that
# covers 3 of 81 filenames is not one.
#
# The two directory rules carry most of the corpus, including the eight lane
# folders whose notes are all named handoff.md in lower case -- the HANDOFF-*
# patterns below are for the root-level ones and are case-sensitive off Windows,
# so the directory rule is what makes the lower-case ones safe.
HIRING_MANAGER_DRESS_REHEARSAL_PROMPT.md
HIRING_MANAGER_NEXT_OPUS_BATCH.md
HIRING_MANAGER_DRESS_REHEARSAL_REPORT.md
DEMO-SCRIPT-*.md
HANDOFF.md
HANDOFF-*.md
docs/rehearsal-review/
docs/dress-rehearsal-*-evidence/

# Operational backups (scripts/backup-state.sh, demos/06_backup_restore.sh).
# Real database and outbox contents, written beside the stack. Never committed.
backups/

# Event re-check evidence ledgers (scripts/event-recheck.sh). An append-only
# record of what each venue page said when it was last opened, written beside
# the stack by the operator who ran the probe. It is local operational
# evidence, not part of the submission.
.recheck/
